      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\n`sglang:http_requests_total`, `sglang:http_responses_total` and `sglang:http_requests_active` are recorded by a middleware over every route, so they also count the orchestrator's probes (`/health`, `/health_generate`, `/ready`, `/ping`) and Prometheus's own `/metrics` scrapes. Two effects:\r\n\r\n- A pod that is still loading answers `/ready` with 503. In an error-rate query such as `sum(rate(sglang:http_responses_total{status_code!=\"200\"}[30s])) / sum(rate(sglang:http_responses_total[30s]))` those count as errors.\r\n- A scrape every second adds one request per second to an idle server, so request rates and the active gauge never read zero.\r\n\r\nMeasured on 2026-10-17 with SGLang v0.5.21 serving Qwen3-8B on an H100: an Argo Rollouts canary check with the query above read 3.2% errors and rolled the new version back, while every one of its 33 chat completions had returned 200. The 503s were three readiness probes during warm-up, out of about 90 responses, most of them `/metrics` scrapes. A healthy version would have been rolled back the same way.\r\n\r\nCompanion to #45211, from the same measurement; the two are independent.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- `HTTP_METRICS_EXCLUDED_PATHS` in `sglang/srt/observability/http_request_metrics.py` names the probe and scrape paths the server serves; `track_http_status_code` passes those requests through without touching the three metrics. Client traffic is counted exactly as before.\r\n- Unit tests in `test/registered/unit/observability/test_http_request_metrics.py`: the middleware on a small FastAPI app counts a chat completion and not `/ready`, `/health` or a `/metrics` scrape (metrics mocked, so the existing test's uninitialized-metrics check still holds); every excluded path other than `/metrics`, which is mounted at startup, is a route on the server's app.\r\n\r\nProbe outcomes stay observable where they already are: the readiness and liveness state in Kubernetes, and the server log. If an opt-in flag is preferred over a changed default, the set can become a `--metrics-exclude-paths` argument with the same default.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nNot applicable: metrics only.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nNot applicable: one set lookup per request in the middleware.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format your code according to the Format code with pre-commit guide (ruff, ruff-format, isort, codespell run on the changed files).\r\n- [x] Add unit tests.\r\n- [ ] Update documentation: `docs/docs/references/production_metrics.mdx` doesn't describe the HTTP counters today; happy to add a short section if wanted.\r\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results: not applicable.\r\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39652275099](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39652275099)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39652274256](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39652274256)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39652274421](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39652274421)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
